Source: pg-kv
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~), cargo, clang, libicu-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/Murat7Ay/pg_kv

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-kv
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-kv
Depends: postgresql-PGVERSION, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Shared-memory key/value cache, rate limits and sorted sets
 pg_kv provides a shared-memory key/value cache with TTL, token-bucket rate
 limits and sorted sets. It requires shared_preload_libraries and uses one
 nontransactional, nonpersistent keyspace across all databases in the cluster.
 This is an early upstream release, not intended for production use.
